<form class="form-horizontal">
  <div class="alert">
    Every value here ends up in a move or decides when the head stops going down. The plugin
    checks each value when you save and again before each job. It never sends laser, fan or
    heater commands.
  </div>

  <h4>Probe device</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">ESP base URL</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.esp_url">
      <span class="help-block">The ESPHome probe controller. Its REST API must be reachable from the OctoPrint host.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">HTTP timeout, s</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.http_timeout">
      <span class="help-block">For each request. A failed read of the probe latch is tried once more, then stops the job. Display updates never stop a job.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Arm wait, s</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.arm_wait_s">
      <span class="help-block">Wait after deploying the pin before the latch is cleared and checked. The deploy pulse lasts 0.68 s, so 0.7 s is the least.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Heights</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Safe Z, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.safe_z">
      <span class="help-block">No default: capture it on the tab (jog, then Use current Z). Travel happens at this height or higher: a head above it travels where it is. It must clear the tallest part of the object with the pin deployed.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Z floor, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.z_floor">
      <span class="help-block">No default: deploy the pin, jog its tip to just above the bed or fixture, and capture it on the tab. No probing step goes below this. At least 0: soft endstops clamp Z at 0 without telling anyone.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Max descent, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.max_descent">
      <span class="help-block">An extra bound: no probing step goes further than this below safe Z.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Probe here window, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.here_max_descent">
      <span class="help-block">Probe here lowers the head at most this far below where you left it (and never below the Z floor, if one is set). Jog to a few mm above the spot first.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Probe square default</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.here_square_size"> mm,
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.here_square_n"> points per side
      <span class="help-block">The square Probe here starts with (0.5 to 50 mm, 2 to 9 points per side). It reports the highest point.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Height map tolerance</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.05" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.map_tolerance"> mm
      <span class="help-block">The plugin warns when the printer's 28 mm mesh misses a probed height by more than this (0.02 to 5 mm). Use roughly how far your laser can be out of focus before the burn changes.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Laser focus gap</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="0.5" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.map_focus_gap"> mm
      <span class="help-block">The distance from the lowest part of the laser module to its focus. With it, the plugin warns when an object's height range is so big that a lost height map would put the head into the tallest part. Leave empty if unknown.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Stages</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.stages">
      <span class="help-block">&quot;step, start_above&quot; for each stage, coarse first, separated by ;. The first stage starts at safe Z. Each later stage starts start_above over the last trigger, and start_above must be more than its own step.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Samples</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Samples</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.samples">
      <span class="help-block">Fine measurements that must agree for each point, the first included.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tolerance, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.tolerance">
      <span class="help-block">How closely they must agree.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Max samples</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.max_samples">
      <span class="help-block">If they do not agree, take more, up to this many. Then the point fails.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Speeds</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Probe feed, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.probe_feed">
      <span class="help-block">Each probing step (G1).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Z travel feed, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.z_feed">
      <span class="help-block">Rises and the moves between stages (G0).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">XY travel feed, mm/min</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.xy_feed">
      <span class="help-block">Travel at safe Z (G0).</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Job</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.home_first">
        Home (G28) before each job
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">G28 homes Z upwards on this machine. After homing, the first point probes its way down from the top, which takes a while.</span>
      <span class="help-block">Off only if the machine is already homed and nothing moved it by hand.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.tap_test">
        Tap test before every automatic job and calibration
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">Probe here always needs one tap test per session (and again after the probe board restarts), whatever this says.</span>
      <div class="alert alert-error">
        <strong>Leave this on.</strong> The tap test is the only check that a touch really
        reaches the ESP today. If the signal path is dead, the probe trips on the object and
        nobody hears it: the head keeps stepping down until the Z floor. The probe's own wiring
        test cannot stand in for it, because some clones have no touch mode.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Laser modules</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Modules</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <textarea rows="4" class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.laser_modules"></textarea>
      <span class="help-block">
        One per line: <code>name = focus offset, dx, dy</code> in mm, any field blank until
        measured (<code>10W = , 0, 0</code>, <code>2W IR =</code>). Focus Z = trigger Z + focus
        offset. dx, dy is the probe pin's position minus that module's beam: the head goes to
        (X - dx, Y - dy). The pin is built on the 10W's axis, so 10W is 0, 0; the IR beam sits
        elsewhere and stays blank (a warning) until measured. The tab fills these in.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.lightburn_invert">
        Flip the sign of the LightBurn Z offset column
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Off: positive means the point is higher than the datum, so the head must go up.
        LightBurn's docs say a positive cut-setting Z Offset moves the head towards the
        material, and its Reverse Z device setting swaps that. Check the direction once with
        the beam off.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>LightBurn bridge</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Enabled</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_enabled"> Answer as a GRBL laser for LightBurn</label>
      <span class="help-block">Turning it on or off, or changing the port, takes effect after an OctoPrint restart.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">TCP port</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_port">
      <span class="help-block">LightBurn's GRBL Ethernet/TCP device points at this port on this computer.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Allowed addresses</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_allow">
      <span class="help-block">IPv4 addresses, comma separated, that may connect. GRBL has no login, so this list (and a firewall rule on this computer) is the access control. See the README, Access and authentication.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Beam offset, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-prepend input-append"><span class="add-on">X</span><input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_offset_x"><span class="add-on">Y</span><input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_offset_y"><span class="add-on">mm</span></div>
      <span class="help-block">Added to LightBurn's X and Y for flat jobs (with the module's own offset), so LightBurn's 0,0 is where the beam lands.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">X backlash, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_backlash_x">
      <span class="help-block">How far short the head stops when it arrives moving +X; flat jobs add it back. Measured 0.52 mm with split-line burns on 22 Nov 2026. 0 turns the correction off.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Arm time, minutes</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_arm_minutes">
      <span class="help-block">Arm the laser for this long at most; it disarms itself after, or when the door opens.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Segment length, mm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bridge_seg_mm">
      <span class="help-block">Long moves are split this short so a stop or a door opening takes effect quickly.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Pointer power</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.pointer_s_max"> of 255, off after <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.pointer_minutes"> min
      <span class="help-block">The 10W's beam as a pointer for LightBurn's Fire button and framing: capped this low, and switched off by itself.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Air purifier</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_enabled">
        Run the purifier for laser jobs</label>
      <label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_enclosure_fan">
        Run the enclosure fan at full speed with it (it blows into the purifier's hose and uses no filter)</label>
      <span class="help-block">It counts the laser energy each job commands (time x power x the module's watts) and
        starts the purifier once a job passes the start energy, or at once if the air sensor sees heavy smoke. After
        the last burn it runs until the air is bearable again (not clean), within the run-on limits. Paper marks
        (about 10 J) never start it.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Home Assistant</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" autocomplete="off" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_ha_url">
      <span class="help-block">Where the purifier's socket and the air sensor live, for example <code>http://homeassistant.local:8123</code>.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Home Assistant token</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="password" class="input-xlarge" autocomplete="off" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_ha_token">
      <span class="help-block">A long-lived access token (your Home Assistant profile, Security). Empty: no socket and no air readings; the fan alone runs on a timer from the job's energy, and only if the socket is already on.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Socket switch</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" autocomplete="off" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_switch">
      <span class="help-block">The switch that powers the purifier, for example <code>switch.laser_purifier</code>.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">PM2.5 sensor</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" autocomplete="off" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_pm25">
      <span class="help-block">Inside the enclosure, for example <code>sensor.pm_2_5mm</code> (Printmonitor2).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Formaldehyde sensor</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" autocomplete="off" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_hcho">
      <span class="help-block">Optional, for example <code>sensor.formaldehyde</code>.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Start energy</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_start_j">
        <span class="add-on">J</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Laser energy in a job before the purifier starts. 300 J is 10 W at full power for 30 s, or about 100 s at 30 %.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Smoke alarm</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_alarm_pm25">
        <span class="add-on">&micro;g/m&sup3;</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">PM2.5 over the air before the job that starts it whatever the energy.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bearable PM2.5</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_pm25_margin">
        <span class="add-on">&micro;g/m&sup3;</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Over the air before the job: the run-on stops once two readings in a row are under this (and under the formaldehyde margin).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bearable formaldehyde</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_hcho_margin">
        <span class="add-on">&micro;g/m&sup3;</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Over the air before the job.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Run-on at least</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_runon_min_s">
        <span class="add-on">s</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">After the last burn.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Run-on at most</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_runon_max_s">
        <span class="add-on">s</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">After the last burn, whatever the sensor says: the filter is precious.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Smoke decay time</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.purifier_tau_s">
        <span class="add-on">s</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Learnt from each run-on (how fast the smoke falls with the purifier on). Used for the timer when the sensor is quiet. Leave empty to learn it again.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4>Head camera and close-ups (10W)</h4>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Overview photo from</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-prepend input-append"><span class="add-on">X</span><input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.headcam_x"><span class="add-on">Y</span><input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.headcam_y"><span class="add-on">Z</span><input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.headcam_z"><span class="add-on">mm</span></div>
      <span class="help-block">Where the head takes the whole-bed photo the close-up box is drawn on. Z 200 or higher (it moves up first).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Photo quality</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.headcam_quality">
      <span class="help-block">The touchscreen's photoQuality: 8 takes about 4 s a photo and is as sharp for the close-up as 1 (12 s).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Photo time, s</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_capture_s">
      <span class="help-block">How long one photo takes, for the time estimates.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Most tiles</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="number" step="1" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_max_tiles">
      <span class="help-block">A close-up needing more photos than this is refused: draw a smaller box or stand further off.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Touchscreen address</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.headcam_url">
      <span class="help-block">The Snapmaker touchscreen's HTTP server, for example
        <code>http://192.168.1.60:8080</code>. The 10W's camera reaches only the touchscreen. Empty: off.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Stand-off</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_standoff">
        <span class="add-on">mm</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">How high the head goes above the object's top for a close-up. The camera is sharp from about 40 to 60 mm (Z45 is the lowest calibrated).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Close-up resolution</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_dpm">
        <span class="add-on">px/mm</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Of the image LightBurn gets (the close-up camera). 15 matches the camera at Z50; LightBurn took up to 20.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tile overlap</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_overlap">
        <span class="add-on"></span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Fraction (0.1 to 0.5) neighbouring photos share.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Head shadow band</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_shadow_frac">
        <span class="add-on"></span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">The least share of each photo's right side treated as the head's shadow when photos are blended (0.4 = 40 %); each photo's own shadow widens it. The tile plan uses the shadow measured on this machine at night in room light (2026-11-21): in daylight or under other lamps it may differ.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Hood clearance</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_min_clearance">
        <span class="add-on">mm</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">The least gap allowed between the 10W's hood and the tallest thing under the module.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Module margin</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_hood_radius">
        <span class="add-on">mm</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Added all round the 10W's outline (from Snapmaker's CAD: 74 mm to the camera side of the beam, 40 to the other, 37 front and back) for the dashed area on the tab.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Approach</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-append">
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_approach_mm">
        <span class="add-on">mm</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Every photo position is reached from -X, -Y by this much (the X axis has about 0.4 mm of backlash).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_fresh_overview">
        Take a fresh overview at the start of every close-up
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">So the close-up is built on the bed as it is now. About 20 s longer.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.burn_closeup_after">
        Take a close-up of the burned area after each LightBurn burn
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">Once a flat burn has finished and the bridge has been idle for 10 s, the 10W photographs the burned area (plus 5 mm round it) and keeps it in Recent burns on the Burn tab. It disarms the laser, as any close-up does.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Close-up base</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <select class="input-xlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.closeup_base">
        <option value="headcam">10W head camera overview (from X232 Y178 Z290)</option>
        <option value="usb">Fixed USB bed camera</option>
      </select>
      <span class="help-block">The whole-bed picture the sharp close-up tiles are blended over. The tiles always come from the 10W. The USB bed camera needs its own calibration first (the <code>bedcam_calibrate</code> command, see the README).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bed camera snapshot</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-xxlarge" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bedcam_url">
      <span class="help-block">A JPEG snapshot URL, for example go2rtc's <code>http://octopi.local:1984/api/frame.jpeg?src=bed_cam</code>.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Bed camera park</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="input-prepend input-append">
        <span class="add-on">X</span>
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bedcam_park_x">
        <span class="add-on">Y</span>
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bedcam_park_y">
        <span class="add-on">Z</span>
        <input type="number" step="any" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: settings.plugins.laserheightprobe.bedcam_park_z">
        <span class="add-on">mm</span>
      </div>
      <span class="help-block">Where the head waits for the bed camera's photo: out of its view, with the bed at the Y the camera was calibrated at (the bed moves in Y under it). Y must match the calibration. Z 200 or higher. Refused with the rotary fitted.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
